# 必考词 Unit27
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit27核心高频词汇

{{designate}}{/ˈdezɪɡneɪt/}}{v. 指定；命名}}{{The area was designated as a national park in 1990.}}

{{detach}}{/dɪˈtætʃ/}}{v. 分离；拆下}}{{She tried to detach herself emotionally from the situation.}}

{{detect}}{/dɪˈtekt/}}{v. 发现；探测}}{{The device can detect minute changes in pressure.}}

{{deteriorate}}{/dɪˈtɪəriəreɪt/}}{v. 恶化；退化}}{{The patient's condition deteriorated rapidly overnight.}}

{{devise}}{/dɪˈvaɪz/}}{v. 设计；发明}}{{The team devised a plan to reduce costs without裁员.}}

{{diagnose}}{/ˈdaɪəɡnəʊz/}}{v. 诊断}}{{The disease was diagnosed at an early stage.}}

{{diminish}}{/dɪˈmɪnɪʃ/}}{v. 减少；缩小}}{{The importance of traditional media has diminished.}}

{{discern}}{/dɪˈsɜːrn/}}{v. 辨别；识别}}{{It was difficult to discern the truth from the conflicting reports.}}

{{disclose}}{/dɪsˈkləʊz/}}{v. 揭露；透露}}{{The company failed to disclose its financial difficulties.}}

{{discourse}}{/ˈdɪskɔːrs/}}{n. 论述；话语}}{{The academic discourse on climate change has evolved significantly.}}

{{discrepancy}}{/dɪˈskrepənsi/}}{n. 差异；矛盾}}{{There is a discrepancy between the two reports.}}

{{discriminate}}{/dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt/}}{v. 区分；歧视}}{{It is wrong to discriminate against people on the basis of gender.}}

{{displace}}{/dɪsˈpleɪs/}}{v. 取代；使流离失所}}{{The flood displaced thousands of families from their homes.}}

{{dispose}}{/dɪˈspəʊz/}}{v. 处理；布置}}{{The company disposed of its waste in an environmentally friendly way.}}

{{disrupt}}{/dɪsˈrʌpt/}}{v. 扰乱；破坏}}{{The storm disrupted transportation across the region.}}

{{dissolve}}{/dɪˈzɒlv/}}{v. 溶解；解散}}{{Parliament was dissolved ahead of the general election.}}

{{distort}}{/dɪˈstɔːrt/}}{v. 歪曲；扭曲}}{{The media can sometimes distort the facts to attract attention.}}

{{distress}}{/dɪˈstres/}}{n. 痛苦；v. 使苦恼}}{{The news of the disaster caused great distress to the families.}}

{{diverge}}{/daɪˈvɜːrdʒ/}}{v. 分歧；偏离}}{{Opinions diverge on the best approach to education reform.}}

{{doctrine}}{/ˈdɒktrɪn/}}{n. 教义；学说}}{{The doctrine of free speech is fundamental to democracy.}}

{{domain}}{/dəˈmeɪn/}}{n. 领域；域}}{{She is an expert in the domain of artificial intelligence.}}

{{donate}}{/dəʊˈneɪt/}}{v. 捐赠；捐献}}{{The billionaire donated millions to charity.}}

{{dwell}}{/dwel/}}{v. 居住；详述}}{{Do not dwell on past failures; focus on the future.}}

{{dynamic}}{/daɪˈnæmɪk/}}{adj. 动态的；有活力的}}{{The dynamic economy of the region attracts many investors.}}

{{elaborate}}{/ɪˈlæbərət/}}{adj. 精心的；v. 详细阐述}}{{The professor asked the student to elaborate on her观点.}}

{{elicit}}{/ɪˈlɪsɪt/}}{v. 引出；诱出}}{{The comedian's jokes elicited loud laughter from the audience.}}

{{eligible}}{/ˈelɪdʒəbl/}}{adj. 有资格的；合格的}}{{Only citizens over 18 are eligible to vote.}}

{{embed}}{/ɪmˈbed/}}{v. 嵌入；使深留脑中}}{{The values are deeply embedded in the culture.}}

{{embody}}{/ɪmˈbɒdi/}}{v. 体现；代表}}{{The constitution embodies the principles of democracy.}}

{{emerge}}{/ɪˈmɜːrdʒ/}}{v. 出现；浮现}}{{New challenges emerge as the company grows.}}

{{empirical}}{/ɪmˈpɪrɪkl/}}{adj. 经验的；实证的}}{{The theory is supported by empirical evidence.}}

{{encompass}}{/ɪnˈkʌmpəs/}}{v. 包含；包围}}{{The course encompasses a wide range of topics.}}

{{endorse}}{/ɪnˈdɔːrs/}}{v. 支持；赞同}}{{The celebrity endorsed the new product in a commercial.}}

{{enforce}}{/ɪnˈfɔːrs/}}{v. 执行；强制}}{{The police enforce the law to maintain public order.}}

{{enhance}}{/ɪnˈhɑːns/}}{v. 增强；提高}}{{The new software enhances the user experience.}}

{{enlighten}}{/ɪnˈlaɪtn/}}{v. 启发；开导}}{{The lecture enlightened the audience about the history of art.}}

{{enrich}}{/ɪnˈrɪtʃ/}}{v. 使丰富；充实}}{{Travel can enrich your understanding of different cultures.}}

{{enroll}}{/ɪnˈrəʊl/}}{v. 登记；注册}}{{She enrolled in a master's program at the university.}}

{{ensue}}{/ɪnˈsjuː/}}{v. 接着发生；继起}}{{A heated debate ensued after the announcement.}}

{{enterprise}}{/ˈentərpraɪz/}}{n. 企业；事业}}{{Entrepreneurial enterprise drives economic growth.}}
